## 2. Users and roles

Every person sees a different product depending on who they are. Design each role as its own experience, not as a hidden-menu version of the manager screen.

### 2.1 Roles and personas

"Admin" is no longer used for business staff. **Platform admin** means our own team. **Manager** means the business's front-desk or operations person.

| Role | Who they are | Main device | Goal | Frustration today | What they see and do |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Platform admin | Our own team | Web | Keep businesses running | Not applicable | Manages all businesses, plans, billing and support. Internal tool, lowest design priority. |
| Business owner | Founder or top admin of one business | Web and phone | Know what is late, owed and paid | Cannot see who has paid. Counts wages by hand. | Sets up the business, creates staff, sees all orders, money and reports, reviews wages. |
| Manager | Front-desk or operations person | Web and tablet | Take orders without mistakes | Lost orders, repeated "is it ready?" calls | Takes orders, records customers and measurements, creates and assigns tasks, verifies finished work, issues invoices, records payments. |
| Worker | Tailor, ironer, packer (barber and others later) | Phone (often low-end Android) | Know the next job, get paid correctly | Disputes about what was done and what is owed | Sees only assigned tasks, updates progress, marks work done, sees own earnings. |
| Cashier | Front-desk or payment person | Web and tablet | Record payments accurately and quickly | Manual receipt writing | Records cash and transfer payments, issues receipts, views orders and invoices. Cannot create orders or assign tasks. |
| Customer | Person buying from the business | Phone, via WhatsApp link | Know when the order is ready and what is owed | Having to call to ask for status | Tracks progress, receives invoices, sees balance. Pays the business directly, not through the platform. |
| Supplier | Fabric seller, equipment vendor | Phone and web | Get orders and be paid | Chasing payments | Phase 3. Runs a small shop on the platform, receives orders and sends payment requests for accepted orders. |
| Subcontractor | External tailor or finisher | Phone | Receive work and update it | Unclear instructions | Phase 2B. Receives outsourced tasks with a limited login. |
| Delivery partner | Third-party rider or logistics company | Phone | Complete deliveries | Unclear drop-off details | Phase 3. Receives delivery requests and confirms drop-off. |

### 2.2 Permission matrix

Permissions are enforced on the server for every request. Hiding a menu item is not security.

| Data | Owner | Manager | Cashier | Worker | Customer (via link) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| All orders | Yes | Yes | View only | No | Own order only |
| Assigned tasks | Yes | Yes | No | Own tasks only | No |
| Customer full details (phone, address) | Yes | Yes | No | No | Own only |
| Customer first name | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes (on assigned tasks) | Own only |
| Measurements and fabric photos | Yes | Yes | No | Yes (on assigned tasks) | No |
| Edit or delete saved measurements | Yes | Yes | No | No | No |
| Invoices and payments | Yes | Yes | View and record | No | Own invoice and balance |
| Record cash or transfer payment | Yes | Yes | Yes | No | No |
| Pay rates and wage run | Yes | No | No | Own earnings only | No |
| Staff list and roles | Yes | View only | No | No | No |
| Business settings and branding | Yes | No | No | No | No |
| Reports | Yes | Yes (orders and balances only) | No | No | No |

### 2.3 Access rules

- The owner creates staff accounts by entering the worker's **phone number**. Staff do not self-register.
- Staff sign in with a **one-time code** sent by SMS or WhatsApp on first use, then a **PIN** on that device. Nobody is ever sent a password. The owner can revoke any device. A forgotten PIN is reset with a new one-time code.
- A worker never sees other workers' tasks, a customer's phone number or address, or business finances.
- A customer never needs a password for basic tracking. A link from WhatsApp is enough. The link contains a **random, unguessable token** (never the order number). The page shows first name, stages, balance and pickup details only. The manager can regenerate the link to cancel an old one.
- A customer account is optional and only needed to see history across orders (Phase 2B).
- Roles are customizable per business in Phase 2A (for example, a barbing salon calls workers "stylists").

