## 8. Phase 4: Scale and ecosystem

These are directional ideas, not a commitment. Design does not need to start here, but four decisions made in Phase 1 must leave room for them.

**Four rules for Phase 1 that protect Phase 4**

1. Phone numbers are stored in international format, so people can be matched later.
2. Customer records and measurements belong to one business. Sharing across businesses needs the customer's consent.
3. Every task stores its start time and finish time.
4. Every record carries its business, and nothing assumes a single location.

| Idea | What it would do | Note |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Native customer app | One app where a customer follows orders across every business. | Needs a customer identity outside one business. |
| Shareable profile | A customer's measurements carried across businesses, with permission. | Consent required. |
| Marketplace | Customers discover nearby businesses by type and location. | Customer discovery only. Supplier connections stay invite-only. |
| Smart assignment | Suggestions that learn which worker finishes which kind of task fastest. | Uses the task times from rule 3. See §13. |
| Multi-branch businesses | One owner, several locations, branch managers, branch-level reports. | |
| Loyalty and promotions | Points, discounts and campaigns to past customers. | |
| Integrations | Accounting tools, more payment providers, SMS and other messaging channels. | |
| Business financing | Using payment and order history to offer working-capital options. | **Subject to legal review.** |
| Open API and app store | Let other developers build add-ons. | |
| Offline-first worker app | Full offline operation with conflict handling. | Phase 1 has the limited offline mode in §4.2. |

