## 10. Notifications, messaging and pricing touchpoints

Most customers will meet the product through WhatsApp messages and the tracking page before they ever see a full screen. Treat these as designed surfaces.

### 10.1 Messages to design

This table is the single list. §5.1 refers to it.

| Message | To | Channel | Phase |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Order confirmed, with summary and tracking link | Customer | WhatsApp | 1 |
| Invoice, with bank details and tracking link | Customer | WhatsApp | 1 |
| Payment received, with receipt | Customer | WhatsApp | 1 |
| Stage update (only for stages the business marks visible) | Customer | WhatsApp | 1 |
| Your clothes are ready, with balance due and pickup or delivery details | Customer | WhatsApp | 1 |
| Payment reminder for outstanding balance (one the day after the due date, then weekly, maximum 3; manager can switch off per order) **[CONFIRM]** | Customer | WhatsApp | 1 |
| New task assigned, task due soon (24 hours before due), rework requested | Worker | In app and push | 1 |
| Late order, failed payment, task on hold | Owner, manager | In app and push | 1 |
| Staff one-time login code | Staff | SMS or WhatsApp (SMS allowed for login codes only) | 1 |
| Booking confirmation and reminder | Customer | WhatsApp | 2B |
| Wage paid, with payslip | Worker | In app and WhatsApp | 3 |
| Supplier payment request and approval | Owner, supplier | In app and WhatsApp | 3 |

**Rules for WhatsApp**

- Templates have length and format limits and must be approved by the provider. **Submit the Phase 1 templates before design is finished**, because approval time is outside our control.
- Keep messages short, in plain language, and include the business name.
- Phase 1 sends from **one platform number**. Messages include the business name.
- Customer consent is recorded at order creation.
- Every message has a delivery status the manager can see (queued, sent, delivered, failed).
- **Fallback.** If a message fails, the order shows a **"Copy tracking link"** button so the manager can paste the link into their own WhatsApp.

### 10.2 Pricing touchpoints

We plan to charge businesses a monthly subscription based on plan tiers (staff numbers and feature access), with a **commission on staff payouts** made through the wallet (rate **[CONFIRM]**). Final prices are not set, so design with placeholders. See §15 for the business model.

- **Phase 1 pilots pay nothing.** Billing starts in Phase 2A.
- A plan comparison screen that explains tiers in plain language.
- Limit messages that feel helpful, such as when a business reaches its staff limit.
- A billing page showing the current plan, next payment date and past invoices.
- Locked features shown clearly with an upgrade path, rather than hidden.

