## 15. Business model

**Model.** A monthly subscription based on plan tiers (staff numbers and feature access), plus a **commission on staff payouts** made through the wallet (rate **[CONFIRM]**). Customers do not pay through the platform, so there is no fee on customer payments.

**Phase 1.** Pilots pay nothing. Staff payouts run through Paga (see §5.6). Subscription billing starts in Phase 2A. The payout commission starts in Phase 3.

**Unknowns that must be resolved before prices are set**

| Item | What we need |
| --- | --- |
| Cost per order | WhatsApp messages (up to six per order), photo storage, SMS login codes. Produce a **cost-per-order sheet** from pilot data. |
| Wallet and fees | Paga's fees are included in the amount charged. Decide how the commission and Paga's fees are shown to the owner before they confirm a payout. Confirm Paga's exact limits, fees, and Sunday payout timing before build. |
| Plan tiers | Tiers must fit the market. Phase 1 targets 3 to 20 staff, so a plan allowing only 5 staff would price out most of the target. Starting placeholder: a plan allowing 10 staff. |
| Willingness to pay | At least 2 of 3 pilot owners name a monthly price they would pay (§16.1, measure 8). |
| Margin check | Subscription plus payout commission must exceed cost per order for a typical business. |

