## 16. Success metrics and gates

All targets below are **starting values [CONFIRM]**. Every one is measured by a recorded event (§12.7) or an observed session, never by self-report alone.

### 16.1 Gate 1: end of Phase 1

Measured across three pilot businesses, with S.I.G as the first.

| # | Measure | Target |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Setup time | Median 60 minutes or less from sign-up to first saved order, observed in 3 businesses |
| 2 | Worker autonomy | At least 90% of task status changes in a week are made by the assigned worker themselves |
| 3 | Customer messages | At least 90% of "ready" WhatsApp messages show as delivered |
| 4 | Dashboard accuracy | Late orders and unpaid balances match the owner's own check every week for 4 weeks |
| 5 | Wage accuracy | Wage run totals differ from the owner's own count by under 2% for 4 straight weeks |
| 6 | Daily use | At least 80% of new orders are entered on the platform for 8 weeks |
| 7 | Fewer status calls | "Is it ready?" calls and messages fall by half against a baseline measured in week 0 |
| 8 | Willingness to pay | At least 2 of 3 pilot owners name a monthly price they would pay |

### 16.2 Gate 2: end of Phase 2

- At least 3 businesses of each of 3 new types complete setup without our team building anything custom, and run for 30 days.
- At least **[N]** of them pay a subscription.

### 16.3 Gate 3: end of Phase 3

- Staff are paid through the platform with no cash counting for 4 straight weeks in at least **[N]** businesses.
- A pilot tailor orders fabric from at least **[N]** of their own existing suppliers who joined the platform, and pays there.

